{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"candidate_id\": \"ba425dde3d5b5c2a4d83f96acbcaca3dff792b3c000ec9101309b32a820f24ac\",\n  \"coverage\": [\n    \"Verified connector numbering and saved topology: J1.1–R1.1 input; J1.2–R1.2–C1.1 output; J1.3–C1.2 ground. Sources: inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb:210,359,587; inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch:142,805,835,1091; work/netlist/design.xml, nets.\",\n    \"Computed copper contacts without filtering by assigned net names. Exactly the three expected pad groups were connected, with no cross-net contacts. Checked the output branch intersection and C1 ground return through the via and saved B.Cu fill. Sources: inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb:667–734; review-work/physical/experiments/saved_copper_graph.json, physical_groups and contacts_ignoring_net_names.\",\n    \"Reviewed board outline, courtyard separation, pad gaps and nominal annular dimensions. Calculations, commands, versions, assumptions and outcomes are recorded in review-work/physical/experiments/physical_review_notes.md.\",\n    \"Inspected native check results and their coverage: work/drc/drc.json reports no violations, unconnected items or schematic-parity issues; work/erc/erc.json reports no violations. Explicit contract comparison addresses connector assumptions that schematic parity alone would not test.\"\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Copper contact calculations share KiCad's geometry engine with DRC and assume saved plated interlayer connections. No independent geometry kernel or hardware continuity measurement was used.\",\n    \"Evaluated zone fill as saved; no refill or fresh-fill equivalence check was performed.\",\n    \"Ignored ERC/DRC categories remain coverage omissions; their exact lists are in work/erc/erc.json and work/drc/drc.json and documented in the experiment notes.\",\n    \"No fabrication export review, production tolerance qualification, selected-part fit or mating-connector validation was performed.\",\n    \"No electrical stimuli, transfer-response measurements, analog simulation, parasitic/EMC analysis, thermal or ampacity qualification, or environmental qualification was performed. Trace width alone was not used to infer current capability.\"\n  ],\n  \"packet_sha256\": \"3179a59afa98a5be4e1f0515255a850f1332e84ca66fb0953224e1574cba54d0\",\n  \"role\": \"physical\",\n  \"run_id\": \"52cc8472-02ad-402f-a7e0-98d3a2482308\",\n  \"schema\": \"agent-ee.review/1\"\n}"}}
